---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';
---

<Base title="about" description={`About ${SITE.name} — ai + product, ${SITE.location}.`}>
  <div class="page-head wrap">
    <h1>about</h1>
    <p class="sub">the longer version.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="section wrap">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I'm {SITE.name}, an engineer working across <strong>ai</strong> and
        <strong>product</strong>. The short version of the job: figure out what's
        worth building, build it, and ship it — usually somewhere in the messy
        middle where a model's behaviour and a user's expectations meet.
      </p>

      <p>
        Most of my day is product work with a strong engineering bias: turning a
        vague "we should use ai here" into something with a defined input, a
        measurable output, and a feedback loop that keeps it honest. That means a
        lot of prototyping, a lot of evaluation, and a willingness to throw away
        the first three attempts.
      </p>

      <h2>how i work</h2>

      <p>
        I like small surfaces and fast loops. A rough thing in front of a real
        user beats a polished thing in a doc. I write things down — this site is
        part of that habit — because the notes are usually where the next idea
        comes from.
      </p>

      <p>
        On the tools side: TypeScript and Python most days, a static site when a
        static site will do, and as little client-side machinery as I can get
        away with.
      </p>

      <h2>elsewhere</h2>

      <p>
        Based in {SITE.location}. You can find code on
        <a href={SITE.github}>GitHub</a>, and the fastest way to reach me is
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>email</a>. For the snapshot of what I'm
        doing right now, see <a href="/now">/now</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
